    {
      "type": "row",
      "collapsed": false,
      "title": "Write-back and job loss",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 38
      },
      "id": 0,
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "sum(count_over_time({app=\"repo-guardian\"} |= \"store write-back failed\" [15m]))",
          "legendFormat": "repo state"
        },
        {
          "expr": "sum(count_over_time({app=\"repo-guardian\"} |= \"rule-state write-back failed\" [15m]))",
          "legendFormat": "rule state"
        }
      ],
      "title": "State write-back failures",
      "description": "Write-back is best-effort by design — the queue is the source of truth for 'did we do the work' — so these never fail a job and never appear in errors_total. What they do is make every posture gauge on E1 and E2 stale, which is the one failure those gauges cannot report about themselves.",
      "transparent": false,
      "datasource": {
        "type": "loki",
        "uid": "loki"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 9,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 39
      },
      "repeatDirection": "h",
